cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research line in your work, please cite the project registry."
title: "Does the substrate compute? Closed-loop information-theoretic validation of a neuromorphic substrate on the cortical-labs contract for humanoid locomotion"
abstract: >-
  Three-phase research line demonstrating that a spiking neural network trained
  in-silico can carry a load-bearing control task for a humanoid through the
  Cortical Labs API contract, with mutual-information and transfer-entropy
  validation and a measured physical authority envelope.
keywords:
  - neuromorphic computing
  - spiking neural networks
  - wetware
  - cortical-labs-contract
  - closed-loop control
  - humanoid locomotion
  - mutual information
  - transfer entropy
license: MIT
